  "declared_proposition": "Let Q(d) be one when d is a prime power p^k with k>=1 and zero otherwise. Then Omega(n)=sum_(d|n) Q(d). Therefore the n-only arithmetic weight W(n)=2-(3/2)Omega(n) exactly realizes the TICKET-204 formal signs: W(p)=1/2 on primes and W(pq)=-1 on semiprimes, including squares. This signed realization does not solve the parity problem: W(n)W(n+2)>0 also on infinitely many forced composite-composite pairs.",
