  "mathematical_argument": "If n=product p^e, its prime-power divisors for a fixed p are exactly p,p^2,...,p^e, so the divisor sum contributes e and totals Omega(n). Substitution gives the prime and P2 signs. For n=3+15k with k>=2, n is a proper multiple of 3 and n+2 is a proper multiple of 5. Both have Omega at least two, hence both W values are negative and their shift-two product is positive although neither endpoint is prime.",
